<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#obelisk">Glossary</a> · Term</p><h1 class="enc-title">Obelisk</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">An obelisk is a tall, narrow, tapering stone monument, often carved from a single block. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aksumite-empire">Aksumite Empire</a>, monumental stelae of this kind were erected at the capital Aksum, the largest standing over 33 metres tall according to the profile. These carved stelae served as royal funerary markers and demonstrate Aksum's engineering and organisational sophistication.</p></div>
